between the dragon ball super manga goku  jumping off the battle bus and fortnite  and the release of dragon ball super  superhero it's a good time to love  dragon ball how goes it everyone i'm red  muffler man since rob's hibernating in  the sand healing chamber after staying  up all night to watch she-hulk i'll be  the one talking about dragon ball super  superhero giving my general thoughts on  it and covering any small details you  might have missed along the way so let's  get into it to start with the movie  opens up with this gorgeous hand-drawn  animated set piece running down the  origin of the red ribbon army who were  one of the main baddies in the original  dragon ball showing characters who  haven't been drawn in a modern dragon  ball style for a very long time  commander blue officer black and even  smaller bit characters like android 8.  they even show goku blowing up mercenary  tao the intro also briefly goes over the  events of the android saga the death of  dr ghetto and of course the birth of  cell and seeing cell drawn in the modern  dragon ball style was honestly a real  treat for me especially since both  toriyama and toei have gone on records  saying they go out of their way to not  draw cell anymore because his spots make  him way too difficult to draw  consistently so yeah if you've ever  wondered why frieza was allowed to come  back and not sell well there's your  answer but from here we're introduced to  our uh big baddie magenta the son of  commander rad who is in charge of the  red ribbon army back in dragon ball and  much like his father he wants to bring  the army back into prominence and like  everyone else in the red ribbon army he  is named after a color god i love  toriyama naming conventions goku  literally named his son food and then we  have dr heto the grandson of dr ghetto  and i love this dude fun fact dr heto's  name is meant to be a play on words for  nausea medication while dr ghetto's name  essentially translates to dr vomit but  his name isn't the only thing that's the  polar opposite of his granddad while  ghetto wanted to build androids for the  purpose of world domination pedo is just  a sweet lovable little dork that wants  to make android superheroes he also  stole some corpses to go toward that  research but uh you know who isn't a  little problematic these days magenta  meets with hedo to try to get his  android expertise on his side but at  this point hedo isn't convinced since  working with the red ribbon army isn't  exactly something superman would do so  magenta shows him a video a video  that'll look really familiar to dragon  ball fans it's a candid shot of the  scene where future trunks eviscerates  frieza in real time and i  giggled when i saw this obviously the  original scene had all the flair and  slow pacing you'd expect from old dragon  ball z but seeing trunks just hop up to  frieza and cut him up like fresh sashimi  in two seconds was a really cathartic  way to reframe that scene but yeah the  video convinces heto that the people  running around capsule corporation are  like lizard people or something and he's  like yeah that's good enough of a reason  for me to build super robots for  fascists and from here we move on to  piccolo who's gotten a bit of a design  change his arms have gone from bright  pink to yellow this is because of the  fact that as namekians get older the  color of their uh  arm sacks  began to change so he did it everybody  piccolo finally hit puberty not only  that he's a homeowner has a cell phone  and his bed is covered in a mountain of  plushies he's just like me for real for  real but we see that he's training pan  right now who at this point is three  meaning this movie is placed about a  year off from the end of dragon ball z  where goku just goes off to train with  ub leaving his family behind for like a  decade granted it's not like goku is a  stranger to just leaving his family and  friends for long stretches of time for  shadowing but shortly after this we're  introduced to gamma one and gamma two  these guys are androids and they're the  magnum opus creations of dr hetto as  mentioned earlier hedo's entire  aesthetic is based around superheroes  heroes of justice all that cool and  these guys are all that and more gamma 1  and gamma 2 follow the hero aesthetics  found in tokusatsu and super sentai  shows basically the japanese power  rangers the duo are constantly striking  powerful hero poses with pyrotechnics in  the back as onomatopoeia appear behind  them the words actually appear and  piccolo at one point is even in shock  because of it this is seemingly  explained through the fact that hedo in  order to make his androids as cool as  possible built hologram generators into  their backs the fact that he was this  much of a dork to include this solely  because he watched a lot of power  rangers as a kid is incredible but gamma  1 and gamma 2's relation to tokusatsu  doesn't end there their characterization  even follows a standard formula found in  the genre of super sentai gamma 1 is  level-headed and stoic he acts logically  with the responsibility of a leader  essentially the red ranger meanwhile  gamma 2 acts in the opposite fashion  cracking puns at a moment's notice  living relatively carefree but also  being prone to lashing out in bouts of  emotion many of which are traits found  in secondary rangers the two androids  fight with toyish laser blasters they  fly around with flashy high impact moves  like the inazuma kick or straight up  drop kicking people they are the living  embodiment of the japanese live-action  superhero aesthetic and i love it and  another thing about this movie is that  it really plays with a lot of the tropes  people are used to with dragon ball as a  whole so these gamma androids are real  strong and they're up to no good right  well nothing goku and vegeta can't  handle right well throughout the entire  movie goku vegeta and broly are training  up on the planet of lord beerus while  everyone else there just eats ice cream  and they end up missing all of bulma's  phone calls trying to get goku and  vegeta back to earth this is so  relatable i miss work phone calls like  all the time well that's fine though  since bulma is the dragon ball so they  can just wish away the red ribbon army  right well no because piccolo is petty  and that's an easy way out so instead he  just wishes for the dragon to give him  an awakening of his hidden power akin to  the one gohan and krillin received from  guru then bulma wishes for a toned ass  and longer eyelashes but then realized  they could have just used the dragon  balls to teleport goku and vegeta there  instead this is the kind of slapstick  playing with your expectations that i  expect from classic dragon ball the kind  of story where krillin wins a fight by  farting in a dude's face or oolong  wishing for a pair of underwear i'm  honestly a huge fan of this whimsical  approach to the writing it's very  toriyama then we have gohan and the  first thing i gotta say is this dude  finally found a barber gohan's hair in  super looks so  bad  but gohan's hair isn't the only glow up  this movie overall feels like the send  up to his character that we were  promised during the buu saga gohan  begins the movie soft and out of  practice similar to how he was the  beginning of super but after pan gets  kidnapped weird see gohan get mad and he  and piccolo take the fight to the red  ribbon army and it's here that piccolo  after like 30 years it's a new form  piccolo orange no oh yeah that's orange  alright jokes aside i'm actually a big  fan of this transformation visually it  takes a combination of elements from  piccolo's normal design and gives them  the more chiseled demonic look of king  piccolo his antenna are framed on his  face in such a way that they come off  more as devil horns hearkening back to  his origin in the original dragon ball  as a demon king while he's in this form  they even throw back to piccolo's  ability to grow in size to gigantic  proportions which he used against goku  in the world martial arts tournament but  now moving on to the climax the film's  big reveals that while dr hetto had  built gamma 1 and gamma 2 he was also  forced to produce cell max a successor  to the original cell created by dr  ghetto while the androids are fighting  with gohan and piccolo cell max ends up  getting woken up and this results in  piccolo gohan the gammas and basically  every b-less dragon ball character  trying to stop him and this leads to  something very interesting i noticed  about gamma one and two gamma one and  two are red and blue respectively and on  one hand thematically that is to tie  into the superhero toku aesthetic but  this also likely ties into the japanese  folk legend of the red and blue oni the  story goes that there was once a red oni  who wished to make friends with a  village of humans however the village  shunned him and wanted nothing to do  with the demon the red oni also had his  best friend the blue oni hearing of the  red onis plight the blue only offers to  faint attacking the village in order for  the red oni to step in and stop him in  order to look like a hero to the  villagers the plant succeeds but the red  oni then realizes he can never speak to  the blue oni again lest the villagers  learn that it was a scheme in essence  blue sacrifices himself for red's  happiness and here against cell  gamma 2 sacrifices his life to fatally  weaken cell max and potentially allow  gamma 1 the opportunity to be a hero to  those around him and to seek redemption  this central theme between gamma 1 and 2  is honestly my favorite part of this  entire film and i hope we get to see  more of gamma 1 later on in dragon ball  super's continuation finally we have  gohan's new transformation called gohan  beast they literally made gohan blanco  cannon god also  why is his hair so tall  what the [ __ ]  okay jokes aside this [ __ ] is raw in the  scene where gohan achieves this  transformation it's meant to mirror the  scene where gohan achieved super saiyan  2 against cell after the death of  android 16 shot for shot they recreated  complete with the reflection in gohan's  eyes the red line indicating the snap  gohan's explosion when this happened my  theater went crazy i went crazy gohan is  furious and his design mirrors the super  saiyan 2 design which is such a cool  detail and to top it all off to finish  off cell max he doesn't use the  kamehameha no no no no he uses the  special beam cannon thematically this is  gohan separating himself from his father  and if you look at the context of how  he's been treated in dragon ball in  terms of giving up his spotlight to goku  it's a special kind of cathartic but i  also think the scene solidifies the  respect between piccolo and gohan that  when things were at their worst gohan  chose to use piccolo's technique that  goku may be his father but piccolo is  his master and with that i think i've  rambled long enough here dragon ball  super superhero is a fantastic movie and  i had a blast getting to go on about it  as per usual if you like what we do feel  free to drop a comment hit like and  subscribe to the channel and if you like  me you can follow me on twitch twitter  and youtube at red muffler man and yeah  have a good one everybody take it easy  oh yeah and vegeta be goku in the  sparring match so i guess vegeta is  canonically stronger  i'm the [ __ ] best kakarot

